       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation. Overdoses of this size have caused shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's weight, kidney function, and liver function don't change that.\n\nCould you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg once daily**, sometimes used for frail or elderly patients, or patients with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf 50 mg is correct, for example because of an unusual protocol, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy or the prescriber first.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
